CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[image.png] (https://alueducation.instructure.com/courses/2722/
 files/511003/preview?hidden=1)\n\nDescription:\n\nThis individual assignme
 nt integrates the concepts of networking and digital acceleration\, crucia
 l for startup success in emerging markets. You will develop a comprehensiv
 e strategy that leverages both effective networking and appropriate techno
 logy to address a specific startup challenge. This assignment will allow y
 ou to apply the knowledge and skills gained in Modules 5 and 6\, promoting
  a holistic approach to business development in the African context.\n\nAs
  emerging entrepreneurs\, building a strong network and developing a smart
  digital strategy are critical for your startup's success. This assignment
  challenges you to combine insights from Module 5 (Networking and Ecosyste
 m Development) and Module 6 (Digital Acceleration) to design a practical a
 ction plan. You will identify key people and ecosystem players you need to
  connect with and create a digital strategy to improve your startup's oper
 ations\, online presence\, and growth potential. This exercise emphasizes 
 real-world application — using both relationships and technology to powe
 r your startup forward.\n\nDeliverables:\n\nYou will deliver your strategy
  in two formats:\n\n*\n\nDeliverable 1: Slide Deck: A concise slide deck s
 ummarizing your Networking and Tech Strategy. [8 - 10 slides Max with the 
 Title slide and References & Citations slide]. \n\n*\n\nDeliverable 2: Pr
 esentation: A 5- 10 minute recorded video presentation of your slide deck.
 \n\nKey Activities:\n\n*\n\nStartup Challenge Selection: Choose a startup 
 challenge that your own startup is facing. (e.g. limited market access\, l
 ack of funding\, inefficient operations).\n\n*\n\nIntegrated Networking an
 d Tech Strategy: Develop a strategy that combines networking and technolog
 y to address the chosen challenge. This strategy should have two parts:\n\
 n*\n\nPart 1: Networking Strategy\n\n*\n\nMap your local startup ecosystem
 : Identify 5 important stakeholders (mentors\, advisors\, investors\, incu
 bators\, universities\, local businesses\, tech hubs\, etc.).\n\n*\n\nSele
 ct 3 key people or organizations you plan to connect with in the next 2 mo
 nths.\n\n*\n\nFor each\, explain:\n\n*\n\nWhy you want to connect with the
 m.\n\n*\n\nWhat value you can offer them.\n\n*\n\nHow you will initiate co
 ntact (e.g.\, LinkedIn\, warm introduction\, email\, event).\n\n*\n\nPart 
 2: Digital Strategy\n\n*\n\nChoose a startup idea (real or hypothetical).\
 n\n*\n\nDevelop a basic digital action plan that includes:\n\n*\n\n1-2 dig
 ital tools you will use to improve operations (e.g.\, Trello for project m
 anagement\, Zoho for CRM).\n\n*\n\n1 e-commerce approach to market and sel
 l your product/service in Africa (e.g.\, social commerce on WhatsApp).\n\n
 *\n\n1 emerging technology (fintech\, agritech\, or healthtech) you could 
 integrate to strengthen your business model.\n\n*\n\n1-2 digital marketing
  strategies tailored for African audiences (e.g.\, Instagram Ads\, WhatsAp
 p promotions).\n\n*\n\nStrategic Alignment: Explain how your networking ef
 forts and technology integration strategy will work in synergy to address 
 the startup challenge.\n\n*\n\nReflection: In your slide deck\, include a 
 slide of 100-150 words\, reflects on:\n\n*\n\nWhat is one potential challe
 nge you foresee in building your network or implementing your digital stra
 tegy?\n\n*\n\nWhat steps will you take to overcome this challenge?\n\n*\n\
 nPresentation: Prepare a 5 - 10 minute presentation outlining your integra
 ted Networking and Tech Strategy. The presentation should clearly articula
 te:\n\n*\n\nThe chosen startup challenge.\n\n*\n\nThe relevant stakeholder
 s and networking plan.\n\n*\n\nThe selected technologies and their applica
 tion.\n\n*\n\nHow networking and technology work together in your strategy
 .\n\nSubmission Format:\n\n* Submission Format and guidelines. \n\n* Uplo
 ad the slide deck in PDF format to Canvas by the deadline.\n\n* Font: Aria
 l or Calibri\n\nFont Size:\n\n* Slide Count: 8-10 slides\n\n* Submission F
 ormat: PDF\n\nEvaluation Focus:\n\n*\n\nClear identification of relevant n
 etwork connections and engagement plans.\n\n*\n\nPractical and creative us
 e of digital tools and strategies.\n\n*\n\nAbility to tailor strategies to
  the African startup ecosystem context.\n\n*\n\nCritical self-reflection o
 n possible challenges and solutions.\n\n*\n\nEffective communication of yo
 ur strategy in the presentation.\n\nPlagiarism & Academic Integrity Discla
 imer\n\nAll submissions must be original and properly referenced. Any evid
 ence of plagiarism or unauthorized collaboration will result in penalties\
 , including potential disqualification of the assignment. Use proper citat
 ion formats (APA/Harvard) for all sources\, statistics\, and references. 
