CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:This assessment is a professional development portfolio contain
 ing final drafts of the module’s full body of work. The portfolio is 40%
  of the final course grade. You had the opportunity to work on all materia
 ls throughout the term\; so you should be able to submit final versions of
  the portfolio on time after applying the feedback you were given. This is
  the [_BEL_PSL 1_Template for the Portfolio.pdf] (https://alueducation.ins
 tructure.com/courses/2709/files/512750?wrap=1) to use.  This portfolio wi
 ll include the following :\n\n1. Career Map: \n\n* Choose a specific job 
 title\, industry\, or field you aspire to work in and explain why you want
  to work there\, and state your career objective. \n\n* Conduct research 
 on the requirements\, skills\, and qualifications necessary to attain your
  desired position. \n\n* Include a SWOT Analysis of your skills\n\n* Expl
 ore various career pathways that can lead you towards your goal. This may 
 involve alternative routes that align with your interests and strengths.\n
 \n* Create a visual representation of your career map. You can use diagram
 s\, flowcharts\, or any other graphical format that effectively illustrate
 s your career trajectory. \n\n* Reflect on potential challenges\, obstacl
 es\, and uncertainties you may encounter along the way. Develop strategies
  to overcome these hurdles and stay resilient in pursuit of your goals.\n\
 n* Provide a written explanation accompanying your career map with a concl
 usion of key insights gained from this exercise.\n\n2. Informational Inter
 view: Modify your original informational interview of a person within the 
 industry you are applying to by incorporating the feedback you received on
  Canvas. Explain why you chose the person you interviewed. Please include 
 the manuscript for questions asked and responses. The maximum number of in
 terview questions is 10. You may find this [template] (https://docs.google
 .com/document/d/1j0Uf_DXu-CHo7W7M6G9KVpPn14yDVPZLi5BfwNBTHNk/edit) useful.
 \n\n3. Internships application: Research potential internship positions y
 ou are interested in and/or that could give you relevant skills/experience
  to eventually land the field mentioned in their career map. Apply for at 
 least 3 identified internship positions and submit evidence of having appl
 ied to them along with application materials. Submit the following documen
 ts: \n\nA. Resume or CV: Customized resume for the application. It should
  highlight education\, work experiences\, skills and extracurricular activ
 ities.  Follow the templates and samples provided on canvas. \n\nB. Link
 edIn Profile: Customize your linkedIn profile based on your career objecti
 ve. Your profile should at least highlight your educational and work exper
 iences that are best suited to the role. You have to follow the details we
  have provided.. Please add a link to your profile on the top of the resum
 e. \n\nC. Cover letter for the application: Submit one customized applica
 tion letter submitted to one company following the template and samples we
  provided on canvas. Additionally\, the letter should briefly explain why 
 you are the best fit for the role/position you are applying for. \n\nD. E
 vidence of internship application: You will submit evidence for each of th
 e three internships you have applied for. These can be emails sent with th
 e letter attached\, a  screenshot of an application confirmation email or
  a signed and stamped letter by the company as a proof that they have rece
 ived your application. If you already have an internship\, submit the appl
 ication documents you used\, and the offer letter. That internship should 
 still be valid/ongoing in Jan 2026 during your internship period.\n\n Add
 itional Notes: \n\n* Use this[ rubric] (https://docs.google.com/spreadshe
 ets/d/1c8EIFWjJu8xiK6sdg7Ia5mb6jztY_NCedx5p0Aep4SY/edit?gid=1382634551#gid
 =1382634551) to check the criteria for success\n\n* The order of the compo
 nents/deliverables in the portfolio should match the order in the instruct
 ions above as also shown/ordered on the rubric below.\n\n* Submit your com
 piled portfolio as a PDF document\, which is accessible for grading. \n\n
 * You should also organize the elements of the portfolio in the presented 
 order of the deliverables above.\n\n*  Inaccessible documents are graded 
 zero.\n\n* Ensure that your submission adheres to the formatting guideline
 s. Please check for spelling and grammatical errors.\n\nFORMATTING\n\n* Fo
 nt:  Times New Roman\n\n* Font Size: 12\n\n* Font Color: Black \n\n* Lin
 e Spacing: 1.50 \n\n* Align: Justify texts\n\n 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:E-Portfolio [Professional_Skills_Lab_1]
