DESCRIPTION:[image.png] (https://alueducation.instructure.com/courses/2722/
 files/511009/preview?hidden=1)\n\nCongratulations on completing Week 7 of 
 this course!\n\nThis individual summative assessment is designed to evalua
 te your individual understanding of key entrepreneurial concepts and your 
 ability to apply them to a real-world business idea. You will develop and 
 deliver a 7-10 minute recorded presentation to potential investors\, showc
 asing your comprehensive understanding of your chosen business model and i
 ts potential for success in an emerging market.\n\nThis assessment will al
 low you to demonstrate your ability to:\n\n*\n\nIndividually identify and 
 evaluate a potential business opportunity in an emerging market.\n\n*\n\nI
 ndividually develop a comprehensive Business Model Canvas. Note: As you pu
 t together your BMC\, consider the feedback given to you by your facilitat
 or in the week 3 assignment. \n\n*\n\nApply entrepreneurial tools and met
 hodologies.\n\n*\n\nAnalyze and navigate the challenges and opportunities 
 facing entrepreneurs in emerging markets.\n\n*\n\nCommunicate your busines
 s idea effectively and persuasively.\n\nKey Components:\n\n* You will pres
 ent your developed Business Model Canvas\, demonstrating your ability to a
 pply entrepreneurial tools and methodologies. The canvas should clearly ar
 ticulate your value proposition\, addressing the needs of your target cust
 omers.\n\n* Your business idea should address a real-world problem or need
  within an emerging market. You should demonstrate an understanding of mar
 ket demand\, feasibility\, and potential social impact.\n\n* You will iden
 tify and justify a suitable financing option for your venture\, demonstrat
 ing an understanding of the challenges and opportunities facing entreprene
 urs in accessing resources.\n\n* Your presentation should reflect a compre
 hensive understanding of the entrepreneurial process and its potential for
  economic and social development within emerging markets.\n\nAssessment Cr
 iteria:\n\n*\n\nValue Proposition: Clearly articulate the value propositio
 n of your business and its relevance to your target customer's needs.\n\n*
 \n\nBusiness Model Canvas: Demonstrate a thorough understanding of the Bus
 iness Model Canvas and its application to your business idea.\n\n*\n\nFina
 ncing Options: Demonstrate a clear understanding of your chosen financing 
 option and how it aligns with the needs of your business.\n\n*\n\nCreativi
 ty and Originality: Present a creative and original business idea with a s
 trong potential for success.\n\n*\n\nPresentation Quality: Deliver a profe
 ssional and engaging presentation with clear and concise communication\, e
 ffective use of visuals\, and minimal technical issues.\n\nSubmission Guid
 elines:\n\n* Refine your week 3 BMC and consider the feedback given by you
 r facilitator.\n\n* Record a 7-10 minute presentation using slides to expl
 ain your Business Model Canvas and your chosen financing option. Your vide
 o should be audio-visual\, showing you and the BMC.\n\n* Use tools like Po
 werPoint\, Canva\, Loom\, to create and record the presentation.\n\n* Ensu
 re your presentation clearly introduces your business\, details your Busin
 ess Model Canvas (from Week 3)\, and justifies your selected financing.\n\
 n* Submit your final slide deck (PDF) and the recording link on Canvas by 
 the deadline.\n\nDeliverables:\n\na) Slide deck\n\nb) Video recorded prese
 ntation\n\nPlagiarism & Academic Integrity Disclaimer\n\nAll submissions m
 ust be original and properly referenced. Any evidence of plagiarism or una
 uthorized collaboration will result in penalties\, including potential dis
 qualification of the assignment. Use proper citation formats (APA/Harvard)
  for all sources\, statistics\, and references. 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Business Model Presentation - Entrepreneurial Venture Proposal [Bui
 lding_Startups_and_Creating_Employment_in_Emerging_Markets]
