 tps://alueducation.instructure.com/courses/2722/files/511009/preview?hidde
 n=1" alt="image.png" data-api-endpoint="https://alueducation.instructure.c
 om/api/v1/courses/2722/files/511009" data-api-returntype="File" loading="l
 azy"></span></strong></p>\n<p><strong><span class="selected">Congratulatio
 ns on completing Week 7 of this course!</span></strong></p>\n<p><span clas
 s="selected">This individual summative assessment is designed to evaluate 
 your individual understanding of key entrepreneurial concepts and your abi
 lity to apply them to a real-world business idea. You will develop and del
 iver a 7-10 minute recorded presentation to potential investors\, showcasi
 ng your comprehensive understanding of your chosen business model and its 
 potential for success in an emerging market.</span></p>\n<p><span class="s
 elected">This assessment will allow you to demonstrate your ability to:</s
 pan></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class="selected">Individually identify and 
 evaluate a potential business opportunity in an emerging market.</span></p
 >\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class="selected">Individually develop a comprehen
 sive Business Model Canvas. Note: As you put together your BMC\, consider 
 the feedback given to you by your facilitator in the week 3 assignment.&nb
 sp\;</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class="selected">Apply entrepreneur
 ial tools and methodologies.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class="sele
 cted">Analyze and navigate the challenges and opportunities facing entrepr
 eneurs in emerging markets.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class="selec
 ted">Communicate your business idea effectively and persuasively.</span></
 p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><span class="selected">Key Components:</span>
 </strong></p>\n<ol style="list-style-type: upper-alpha\;">\n<li><span clas
 s="selected">You will present your developed Business Model Canvas\, demon
 strating your ability to apply entrepreneurial tools and methodologies. Th
 e canvas should clearly articulate your value proposition\, addressing the
  needs of your target customers.</span></li>\n<li><span class="selected">Y
 our business idea should address a real-world problem or need within an em
 erging market. You should demonstrate an understanding of market demand\, 
 feasibility\, and potential social impact.</span></li>\n<li><span class="s
 elected">You will identify and justify a suitable financing option for you
 r venture\, demonstrating an understanding of the challenges and opportuni
 ties facing entrepreneurs in accessing resources.</span></li>\n<li><span c
 lass="selected">Your presentation should reflect a comprehensive understan
 ding of the entrepreneurial process and its potential for economic and soc
 ial development within emerging markets.</span></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><s
 pan class="selected">Assessment Criteria:</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\
 n<p><strong><span class="selected">Value Proposition:</span></strong><span
  class="selected"> Clearly articulate the value proposition of your busine
 ss and its relevance to your target customer's needs.</span></p>\n</li>\n<
 li>\n<p><strong><span class="selected">Business Model Canvas:</span></stro
 ng><span class="selected"> Demonstrate a thorough understanding of the Bus
 iness Model Canvas and its application to your business idea.</span></p>\n
 </li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><span class="selected">Financing Options:</span></
 strong><span class="selected"> Demonstrate a clear understanding of your c
 hosen financing option and how it aligns with the needs of your business.<
 /span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><span class="selected">Creativity and 
 Originality:</span></strong><span class="selected"> Present a creative and
  original business idea with a strong potential for success.</span></p>\n<
 /li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><span class="selected">Presentation Quality:</span>
 </strong><span class="selected"> Deliver a professional and engaging prese
 ntation with clear and concise communication\, effective use of visuals\, 
 and minimal technical issues.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><span c
 lass="selected">Submission Guidelines:</span></strong></p>\n<ol style="lis
 t-style-type: decimal\;">\n<li><span class="selected">Refine your week 3 B
 MC and consider the feedback given by your facilitator.</span></li>\n<li><
 span class="selected">Record a 7-10 minute presentation using slides to ex
 plain your Business Model Canvas and your chosen financing option. Your vi
 deo should be audio-visual\, showing you and the BMC.</span></li>\n<li><sp
 an class="selected">Use tools like PowerPoint\, Canva\, Loom\, to create a
 nd record the presentation.</span></li>\n<li><span class="selected">Ensure
  your presentation clearly introduces your business\, details your Busines
 s Model Canvas (from Week 3)\, and justifies your selected financing.</spa
 n></li>\n<li><span class="selected">Submit your final slide deck (PDF) and
  the recording link on Canvas by the deadline.</span></li>\n</ol>\n<p><spa
 n style="text-decoration: underline\;"><strong>Deliverables:</strong></spa
 n></p>\n<p><strong>a) </strong>Slide deck</p>\n<p><strong>b) </strong>Vide
 o recorded presentation</p>\n<p><span><strong>Plagiarism &amp\; Academic I
 ntegrity Disclaimer</strong></span></p>\n<p><span>All submissions must be 
 original and properly referenced. Any evidence of plagiarism or unauthoriz
 ed collaboration will result in penalties\, including potential disqualifi
 cation of the assignment. Use proper citation formats (APA/Harvard) for al
 l sources\, statistics\, and references.&nbsp\;</span></p>
END:VEVENT
